							"documentation": "UC1 Sign Up — one sequence diagram showing the main collaboration and an account-conflict alternative.\nMemberView reads member type and registration information and calls MemberManager.SignUp. MemberManager validates input before checking account uniqueness.\nAlternative 4a — Invalid input: return a failure identifying the information to correct; do not create or save a Member. Account conflict: return an account conflict failure in the accountExists = true operand. The user may correct the information and submit again.\nMain storage flow — accountExists = false permits construction and SaveMember. Return success only after the account, profile and selected role are verified as stored.\nAlternative 5a — Storage error: verify this registration before retry or termination. Account existence alone does not prove that the submitted profile and role were saved. Unresolved verification must not be reported as success.\nDisplay the existing SignUpResult. Successful registration does not log the user in automatically. Input validation, storage-error policy and resubmission are documented here and in the short prose below the diagram. No additional class field, operation, result property or enum is introduced.",
